{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519030-ananasi-s-web-and-other-bonds","id":1519030,"title":"Ananasi's web and other bonds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-28T08:07:44-07:00","id":1519030,"title":"Ananasi's web and other bonds","content":"The only information about ananasi's web is that they have 4 health level and a strength of 9, thanks to the fomori web power we know that when you try to set free you enter a contested roll angainst the web strength.<br /> <br /> There's some point where it lack of details, if you're completely covered of web and cannot move a muscle, the roll is logically supposed to be harder, no? Plus it does not tell if the web can soak damage if you attack it directly, we know it's stronger than steel but that's all<br /> <br /> For other kind of bond are the st supposed to set a strength stats for a contested roll against chains, rope or anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T20:20:16-07:00","id":1519068,"title":"","content":"This I suppose it only raises the difficulty of the test based on the material that holds it, like on a rope it would be difficulty 6 now an iron chain would be difficulty 8, it seems simple, but I think it would be easier to do it that way, the numbers don't need to be these, they are just for reference, in the case of the web, I remember that there was a variation in strength depending on how much you were trapped, in this case heath level 4 applies to a trapped hand or foot, if the body is trapped so it's hearth 6 to 8 and if you have your back against a wall it's health 11, I don't remember for sure, but certainly had a rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T06:02:36-07:00","id":1519106,"title":"","content":"We don't play it with soak in my group, diff 9 is already plenty of a challenge. Also keep in mind that the strength of spider silk is tensile, not hardness. The same way you can slice through a rope of plant fiber, you can slice the silk. Impact and cuts on it are difficult because of the elasticity, deliberate slicing works better (ie, it's slow and takes more time).<br /> <br /> Completely restrained opponents and PCs have a diff 0 to be hit, and can only spend their action to try to break free in our group.<br /> <br /> <br /> There were some instances where we resolved some of the questions narratively:<br /> <br /> - a (severely) cocooned opponent took a fall, which I ruled softened the impact somewhat<br /> - the same enzymes that spiders use to pre-digest their prey also work on webbing, so an Ananasi can dissolve another's web<br /> - the web is flammable. Fire based attacks ignore the difficulty and destroy the silk within a round. Same for some acids that are good at dissolving organic polymers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:25:58-07:00","id":1519418,"title":"","content":"I have particular case in head for webs<br /> <br /> 1) If the pc is covered by it he loose some dice because of the difficulty to move and must roll to get the web off without those dice, each success would give him back 1 die<br /> <br /> 2) What if the character is strong enough to rip the web? The feat of strength table and it's description tell that if a character has the correct strength he can lift, rip and so on anything without needing to roll, a werewolf with strength 10 can rip steel for exemple.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:43:05-07:00","id":1519467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519030-ananasi-s-web-and-other-bonds?p=1519418#post1519418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have particular case in head for webs<br /> 1) If the pc is covered by it he loose some dice because of the difficulty to move and must roll to get the web off without those dice, each success would give him back 1 die</div> </div> </div> </div>That's tricky if the web is adhesive. The Breedbook has the General Level 4 Gift <i>Web Blanket</i> and W20 the Tenere Gift <i>Web Sheet</i>, both have the contested Strength rating of 9. It sounds like a fun mechanic though, so I would say go for it if the webbing is just binding or tangling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519030-ananasi-s-web-and-other-bonds?p=1519418#post1519418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) What if the character is strong enough to rip the web? The feat of strength table and it's description tell that if a character has the correct strength he can lift, rip and so on anything without needing to roll, a werewolf with strength 10 can rip steel for exemple.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fun one. Feats of Strength are meant as a shortcut to skip unnecessary rolls, and as ST you can always make the call to have a roll anyways. I personally would just say Str 10+ is enough to rip Ananasi webbing without a roll, but that's debatable:<br /> <br /> To break free, you have to overcome two parameters: tensile strength and elasticity. Imagine being bound by strong rubber bands; even if you can exert the necessary force to expand them, that doesn't break them unless you stretch them beyond their maximum elasticity. That combines into something called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultimate_tensile_strength\" target=\"_blank\">UTS</a>.<br /> As you can see in the table of the wiki page, different variants of steel have different strengths. Steel cable is a completely different story from sheet steel (&quot;Tear open a steel drum&quot; from the Feat table), and the alloy and girth also factors in. The same is true for spider silk, which depends on species and the kind of silk the spider is producing. For example, the glue strings in a web are a lot more fragile than the frame strings, so prey is enveloped easily but the web doesn't collapse.<br /> <br /> Say you have spider silk with the average 1000 MPa strength from the table and the diameter of the strands is 3 mm.<br /> 3 mm diameter =&gt; 7 mm\u00b2 area<br /> 7 mm\u00b2 * 1000 MPa = 7000 N = 1574 lbf<br /> So, Str 10 would be just the edge case that would warrant a roll <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Bottom line, it's the ST's call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T02:06:03-07:00","id":1519577,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> The web has a effective strength of 9 but you need an effective strength of 10 to rip it? 9 strength would mean the web can hold 600kg at best, so we can assume it would break with higher weight, 10 strength is 750kg. To me that means a strength 9 is supposely enough to rip it, do you say 10 because of the elasticity of the web that would require a bit more strength to overcome ?<br /> <br /> In addition for the tied up situation i had in mind an ananassi that produce more silk to reinforce the web, it would give more health and strength to it but how much? 1 blood point is four health and 9 strength, if another point is added +2 strength and health level seems appropriate and simple for the st to use, no? You seems aquainted with the subject maybe you have an idea on how strengthened the web would become by adding more silk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:21:36-07:00","id":1519613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519030-ananasi-s-web-and-other-bonds?p=1519577#post1519577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The web has a effective strength of 9 but you need an effective strength of 10 to rip it? 9 strength would mean the web can hold 600kg at best, so we can assume it would break with higher weight, 10 strength is 750kg. To me that means a strength 9 is supposely enough to rip it, do you say 10 because of the elasticity of the web that would require a bit more strength to overcome ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm going by gut feeling. There's a general issue with the ST system where dot values translate poorly into concrete values because they are an abstracted, simplified way of measurement. That means you will often find tables that give guideline values that contradict each other. I would say Str 9 vs Str 9 is contested because they are the same values, and you need to have at least one better to skip the roll. If you go by the little math exercise in my previous post, even Str 10 would be contested. It's one of the situations where you have to make a call as ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519030-ananasi-s-web-and-other-bonds?p=1519577#post1519577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition for the tied up situation i had in mind an ananassi that produce more silk to reinforce the web, it would give more health and strength to it but how much? 1 blood point is four health and 9 strength, if another point is added +2 strength and health level seems appropriate and simple for the st to use, no? You seems aquainted with the subject maybe you have an idea on how strengthened the web would become by adding more silk</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a professional, just interested in both material sciences and spiders. I also have an Ananasi player, so some of this popped up before.<br /> <br /> Technically, adding more material increases the tensile strength, so your idea would work. The calculation in my above post was for a <i>single</i> string with 3 mm width. By adding more strings, you increase the total surface area in the formula, and multiply the tensile strength for each additional string. That's only on paper, though. In reality, the stress is never distributed evenly on all the strings, and you get a cascading effect where each of the strings will snap one by one.<br /> <br /> From an in-game perspective I think +2 strength / +1 health is fair for the additional blood point investment. I have to add though, we never had a situation where a victim had much time to struggle: as soon as she caught them, the Ananasi would administer her paralyzing bite, at which point it was pretty much over.<br /> She <i>does </i>have a Crafting specialization for knots (<i>Shibari </i>actually, but don't google that at work) which I ruled can be used to add extra successes to contested rolls for the webbing strength if it is used to incapacitate a victim.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T06:13:02-07:00","id":1519623,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks for the help <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>, it's gonna be usefull in my campaign \ud83d\ude00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T09:46:40-07:00","id":1519754,"title":"","content":"You're welcome! One more data point of interest: spider silk <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toughness\" target=\"_blank\">toughness</a> is about three times higher than that of kevlar. A vest made from the same amount of material as your standard kevlar vest would be three times more effective at stopping bullets.<br /> <br /> There are ongoing experiments to infuse spider silk with metals. So far only minuscle amounts have been produced in labs, since the technique is quite difficult (it's applied on an atomic level). But the material toughness increases tenfold and tensile strength more than doubles. If you have a Mage or sorcerer friend, you can craft some disgustingly effective gear with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}